  "decision_summary": "Predicted high. Direct human absolute F measurements for anthranilic acid/carboxylic acid analogs (diclofenac ~50%, tolfenamic acid ~91-100%) and other challenging carboxylic acid/sulfonamide drugs (telmisartan 42-58%, rigosertib ~35%, celecoxib 20-40%) support F >= 20%. L5 adds mechanistic low permeability and BCRP efflux evidence for related ionized molecules (5-ASA, sulfasalazine), which weakens confidence but is not query-specific and is not a direct F result; C65 offers a possible carrier-mediated absorption mechanism but is also not query-specific. The direct analog F evidence is not overturned, so prediction remains high with low confidence."
}

